  "notes": "Compound of {閉|へい} (to close) + {鎖|さ} (to lock/chain). Implies a formal or official closing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {工場|こうじょう}を{閉鎖|へいさ}する (to close a factory)\n- {道路|どうろ}を{閉鎖|へいさ}する (to close a road)\n- {閉鎖|へいさ}に{追|お}い{込|こ}まれる (to be forced into closure)\n- {閉鎖|へいさ}{的|てき} (closed-minded; insular)\n\nUSAGE:\nThe adjective form {閉鎖|へいさ}{的|てき} means \"closed\" in the sense of being exclusive, insular, or unwelcoming of outsiders — e.g., {閉鎖|へいさ}{的|てき}な{社会|しゃかい} (a closed society).",
